<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Bojalib</PackageId>
    <Description>High-performance algorithms and data structures the BCL lacks: SIMD pdqsort, parallel, radix, string and stable sorts, selection; order-statistic B-tree dictionary and set; Roaring bitmaps; radix-tree Trie with fuzzy and wildcard search; Aho-Corasick multi-pattern search; indexed priority queue, deque, circular buffer, range set, Fenwick tree, interval tree, union-find, LRU cache, tree traversals; Bloom, binary fuse and cuckoo filters, HyperLogLog, Count-Min, TopK, t-digest and MinHash sketches. No dependencies, trimmable, Native AOT compatible.</Description>
    <!-- Lets consumers' trimmed / Native AOT publishes drop the parts they don't use,
         and turns on the analyzers that warn if we write code that breaks that. -->
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
    <!-- Needed only for [module: SkipLocalsInit] (no pointer code): stackalloc'd buffers aren't zeroed first. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <!-- Validates the package on pack against the last release, so any change that would break code compiled
         against it fails to pack. The intended breaks of 3.0.0 are listed in CompatibilitySuppressions.xml; after
         3.0.0 is on nuget.org, set the baseline to 3.0.0 and delete that file. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
    <PackageValidationBaselineVersion>2.0.0</PackageValidationBaselineVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MinVer" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Bojalib.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
